steps.description:
Workaround: send the header on every request yourself instead of relying on the predefined credential. In the HTTP Request node enable "Send Headers" and add a header parameter:
```json
{
  "sendHeaders": true,
  "headerParameters": {
    "parameters": [
      {
        "name": "Authorization",
        "value": "Bearer <your-api-token>"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
Note: `{{ $credentials }}` expressions are NOT available in HTTP Request node parameters, so you cannot reference the stored credential's token here — use a literal header value, or switch the credential to "Generic Credential Type" > "Header Auth" with name `Authorization` and value `Bearer <your-api-token>`, which is applied to every paginated request.

Instead of (or in addition to) the node-level header, add the header inside Options > Pagination so it is attached to each generated page request. With Pagination Mode "Update a Parameter in Each Request", add a second parameter of type `header`:
```json
{
  "paginationMode": "updateAParameterInEachRequest",
  "parameters": {
    "parameters": [
      {
        "type": "qs",
        "name": "page",
        "value": "={{ $pageCount + 1 }}"
      },
      {
        "type": "header",
        "name": "Authorization",
        "value": "Bearer <your-api-token>"
      }
    ]
  }
}
```
